      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T00:45:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If this does stay, one concern: since aosp/4368057, `generic_access_phys()` gets the physical address from `vma_pfnmap_phys()`, which works the slice out from the address (\"as set up by `remap_pfn_range()` and `insert_pfn()`\").\n\nWith an explicit slice the PTE could map a different 4KB, so I think ptrace or `/proc/pid/mem` through `generic_access_phys()` would access a 4KB the process never mapped.",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "15d0d072420a4b3a22d406864b4dff38aa64c7bf",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
